; EzyMap Scalp Mastery V2.1b - EzyMap_V2_1b_STAGE0_BASELINE.set
; STAGE 0 - CONTROL. Both V2.1b inputs set to TRUE, which is the ROLLBACK
; position, not the default. Reproduces the V2.1a zero-confluence trigger
; ladder exactly: all nine sources present, W1 and D1 eligible on BOTH their
; Level1 (S1/D1) and Level2 (S2/D2) levels, and CURRENT_OUTER keeps its
; directional override right plus its retire-every-other-waiting-setup-on-fill
; privilege.
;
; NOTE THE REVERSED POLARITY. In V3.190, V2.0 and V2.1a the baseline set was
; the all-FALSE one. In V2.1b the baseline is the all-TRUE one: both new
; inputs default to the NEW behaviour, so a default-valued binary is already
; the changed EA. Loading this file is what gives you the old EA back.
;
; Only the V2.1b S01-S03 inputs are listed. Load this ON TOP of your V2.1a
; working set - every other input keeps its current value.
;
; Confirm from the OnInit log that you loaded it. This file must produce:
;   V2.1b: CURRENT_MAP/CURRENT_OUTER tier RESTORED (A/B control only) ...
;   V2.1b: W1/D1 Level1 (S1/D1) inclusion RESTORED (A/B control only) ...
;
InpZeroConfAllowCurrentMapTier=true
InpZeroConfIncludeLevel1=true
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S03 (added later than S01/S02) - InpForceMinimumBaseSizing
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S03 added a NOMINAL lot-sizing floor: with it true, LotSizingCapitalUnits()
; never reports less than InpBaseEquity, so an account below 100 deposit units
; still sizes as if it had 100. It DEFAULTS TO TRUE, which is the same
; reversed polarity S01/S02 use, so this control file pins it FALSE to
; reproduce the pre-S03 unfloored formula exactly.
;
; The floor only moves the STARTING TARGET. It reaches no risk or margin
; calculation, so setting it false here does not make this control arm any
; safer or any riskier than the S03 arm - it only changes the nominal target
; on accounts below 100 units. At 100 units or above the two arms are
; arithmetically identical, so an A/B at a normal tester deposit will show NO
; difference from this input alone. That is expected, not a failed load.
;
; S03 also added the DEPLOYMENT GATE BREAKDOWN log line. That is pure
; instrumentation with no input and no rollback switch - it prints in both
; arms and changes no behaviour.
InpForceMinimumBaseSizing=false
